  "full_response": "### **Design Patterns**\nDesign patterns are reusable, well-proven solutions to common problems in software design. They provide best practices for structuring code to improve maintainability, scalability, and flexibility. Design patterns are categorized into three main types:\n\n1. **Creational Patterns** – Deal with object creation mechanisms.\n2. **Structural Patterns** – Focus on class and object composition.\n3. **Behavioral Patterns** – Define communication between objects.\n\n---\n\n## **1. Observer Pattern (Behavioral)**\n**Purpose:** Defines a one-to-many dependency between objects so that when one object (the **subject**) changes state, all its dependents (**observers**) are notified and updated automatically.\n\n### **Key Components:**\n- **Subject (Observable)** – Maintains a list of observers and provides methods to attach/detach them.\n- **Observer** – Defines an update interface for objects that should be notified of changes.\n- **Concrete Subject** – Implements the subject interface and notifies observers when its state changes.\n- **Concrete Observer** – Implements the observer interface and reacts to updates.\n\n### **Example Use Cases:**\n- Event handling systems (e.g., GUI buttons, stock market updates).\n- Publish-subscribe systems (e.g., news feeds, messaging apps).\n\n### **Example (Java-like Pseudocode):**\n```java\ninterface Observer {\n    void update(String message);\n}\n\nclass NewsAgency { // Subject\n    private List<Observer> observers = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public void addObserver(Observer observer) {\n        observers.add(observer);\n    }\n\n    public void notifyObservers(String news) {\n        for (Observer observer : observers) {\n            observer.update(news);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nclass NewsChannel implements Observer { // Concrete Observer\n    @Override\n    public void update(String news) {\n        System.out.println(\"Breaking News: \" + news);\n    }\n}\n\n// Usage:\nNewsAgency agency = new NewsAgency();\nagency.addObserver(new NewsChannel());\nagency.notifyObservers(\"New AI breakthrough!\");\n```\n\n---\n\n## **2. Factory Pattern (Creational)**\n**Purpose:** Provides an interface for creating objects but allows subclasses to alter the type of objects that will be created. It decouples object creation from usage.\n\n### **Key Components:**\n- **Product** – Defines the interface of objects the factory creates.\n- **Concrete Product** – Implements the product interface.\n- **Creator (Factory)** – Declares the",
